IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc13-contract-intimidation`
IMPORT `ccc13-tests-support`

-- ccc13-tests-contract-intimidation.l4 -- tests of ccc13-contract-intimidation.l4 (ss 422 to 427). Expected values are decided from the text.

`ccc13 test the hybrid class` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`
`ccc13 test the employee stops work` MEANS `s 422(2) being the employee of an employer, the person stops work as a result of the failure of the employer and the person to agree on any matter relating to the person’s employment`
`ccc13 test the member stops work` MEANS `s 422(2) being a member of an organization of employees formed for the purpose of regulating relations between employers and employees, the person stops work as a result of the failure of the employer and a bargaining agent acting on behalf of the organization to agree on any matter relating to the employment of members of the organization`
`ccc13 test another reason` MEANS `s 422(2) a reason that is neither`

§ `s 422 criminal breach of contract`
-- inputs of (2): the reason; the stoppage is the only reason; all steps provided by law are taken; the final-settlement provision is complied with
#ASSERT `s 422(2) the person is saved from having wilfully broken a contract within the meaning of subsection (1)` `ccc13 test the employee stops work` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 422(2) the person is saved from having wilfully broken a contract within the meaning of subsection (1)` `ccc13 test the member stops work` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 422(2) the person is saved from having wilfully broken a contract within the meaning of subsection (1)` `ccc13 test the employee stops work` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE     -- the steps provided by law were not taken
#ASSERT `s 422(2) the person is saved from having wilfully broken a contract within the meaning of subsection (1)` `ccc13 test the employee stops work` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE     -- the final-settlement provision was not complied with
#ASSERT `s 422(2) the person is saved from having wilfully broken a contract within the meaning of subsection (1)` `ccc13 test the employee stops work` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE     -- not "by reason only"
#ASSERT `s 422(2) the person is saved from having wilfully broken a contract within the meaning of subsection (1)` `ccc13 test another reason` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- inputs of (1): wilfully breaks a contract; knows or has reasonable cause to believe; the probable consequence; the saving of (2)
#ASSERT `s 422(1) the conduct is the offence of criminal breach of contract` TRUE TRUE `s 422(1) to endanger human life` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 422(1) the conduct is the offence of criminal breach of contract` TRUE TRUE `s 422(1) to cause serious bodily injury` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 422(1) the conduct is the offence of criminal breach of contract` TRUE TRUE `s 422(1) to expose valuable property, real or personal, to destruction or serious injury` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 422(1) the conduct is the offence of criminal breach of contract` TRUE TRUE `s 422(1) to deprive the inhabitants of a city or place, or part thereof, wholly or to a great extent, of their supply of light, power, gas or water` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 422(1) the conduct is the offence of criminal breach of contract` TRUE TRUE `s 422(1) to delay or prevent the running of any locomotive engine, tender, freight or passenger train or car, on a railway that is a common carrier` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 422(1) the conduct is the offence of criminal breach of contract` TRUE TRUE `s 422(1) a probable consequence that is none of those` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 422(1) the conduct is the offence of criminal breach of contract` FALSE TRUE `s 422(1) to endanger human life` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 422(1) the conduct is the offence of criminal breach of contract` TRUE FALSE `s 422(1) to endanger human life` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 422(1) the conduct is the offence of criminal breach of contract` TRUE TRUE `s 422(1) to endanger human life` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE        -- the saving of (2) applies
#ASSERT `s 422(1) the conduct is the offence of criminal breach of contract` TRUE TRUE `s 422(1) to endanger human life` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `ccc13 test the maximum imprisonment by indictment` (`s 422(1) the punishments` `ccc13 test p787`) EQUALS `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`
#ASSERT `s 422(1) the class of the offence` EQUALS `ccc13 test the hybrid class`
#ASSERT `s 422(3) the section bars the proceedings for want of the consent of the Attorney General` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 422(3) the section bars the proceedings for want of the consent of the Attorney General` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 423 intimidation`
#ASSERT `s 423(2) the person does not watch or beset within the meaning of section 423` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 423(2) the person does not watch or beset within the meaning of section 423` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE        -- not for the purpose only of obtaining or communicating information
#ASSERT `s 423(2) the person does not watch or beset within the meaning of section 423` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- inputs of (1): wrongfully and without lawful authority; for the purpose of compelling; the act; the saving of (2)
#ASSERT `s 423(1) the conduct is the offence of intimidation` TRUE TRUE `s 423(1) persistently follows that person` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 423(1) the conduct is the offence of intimidation` TRUE TRUE `s 423(1) uses violence or threats of violence to that person or their intimate partner or children, or injures the person’s property` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 423(1) the conduct is the offence of intimidation` TRUE TRUE `s 423(1) blocks or obstructs a highway` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 423(1) the conduct is the offence of intimidation` TRUE TRUE `s 423(1) besets or watches the place where that person resides, works, carries on business or happens to be` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 423(1) the conduct is the offence of intimidation` TRUE TRUE `s 423(1) besets or watches the place where that person resides, works, carries on business or happens to be` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE       -- (2): attending only to obtain information does not watch or beset
#ASSERT `s 423(1) the conduct is the offence of intimidation` TRUE TRUE `s 423(1) besets or watches the place where that person resides, works, carries on business or happens to be` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 423(1) the conduct is the offence of intimidation` TRUE TRUE `s 423(1) persistently follows that person` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE         -- (2) concerns only (f)
#ASSERT `s 423(1) the conduct is the offence of intimidation` TRUE TRUE `s 423(1) an act that is none of those` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 423(1) the conduct is the offence of intimidation` FALSE TRUE `s 423(1) persistently follows that person` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE         -- not wrongful, or with lawful authority
#ASSERT `s 423(1) the conduct is the offence of intimidation` TRUE FALSE `s 423(1) persistently follows that person` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE         -- not for the purpose of compelling
#ASSERT `ccc13 test the maximum imprisonment by indictment` (`s 423(1) the punishments` `ccc13 test p787`) EQUALS `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`
#ASSERT `s 423(1) the class of the offence` EQUALS `ccc13 test the hybrid class`

§ `s 423.1 intimidation of a justice system participant or a journalist`
#ASSERT `s 423.1(4) the person is a military justice system participant` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 423.1(4) the person is a military justice system participant` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 423.1(4) the person is a military justice system participant` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- inputs of (1): conduct without lawful authority; intent to provoke fear; the target; justice system participant (s 2); military justice system participant (s 423.1(4))
#ASSERT `s 423.1(1) the person contravenes subsection (1)` TRUE TRUE `s 423.1(1) a group of persons or the general public, in order to impede the administration of criminal justice` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 423.1(1) the person contravenes subsection (1)` TRUE TRUE `s 423.1(1) a journalist, in order to impede them in the transmission to the public of information in relation to a criminal organization` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 423.1(1) the person contravenes subsection (1)` TRUE TRUE `s 423.1(1) a justice system participant or military justice system participant, in order to impede them in the performance of their duties` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 423.1(1) the person contravenes subsection (1)` TRUE TRUE `s 423.1(1) a justice system participant or military justice system participant, in order to impede them in the performance of their duties` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 423.1(1) the person contravenes subsection (1)` TRUE TRUE `s 423.1(1) a justice system participant or military justice system participant, in order to impede them in the performance of their duties` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING     -- neither kind of participant: outside the prohibition
#ASSERT `s 423.1(1) the person contravenes subsection (1)` TRUE TRUE `s 423.1(1) a target that is none of those` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 423.1(1) the person contravenes subsection (1)` FALSE TRUE `s 423.1(1) a journalist, in order to impede them in the transmission to the public of information in relation to a criminal organization` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING      -- with lawful authority
#ASSERT `s 423.1(1) the person contravenes subsection (1)` TRUE FALSE `s 423.1(1) a journalist, in order to impede them in the transmission to the public of information in relation to a criminal organization` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING     -- no intent to provoke a state of fear
#ASSERT `s 423.1(2) as the text shows it` EQUALS "(2) [Repealed, 2015, c. 13, s. 12]"
#ASSERT `s 423.1(3) the person is guilty of an offence for contravening section 423.1` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 423.1(3) the person is guilty of an offence for contravening section 423.1` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `ccc13 test the maximum imprisonment by indictment` (`s 423.1(3) the punishments`) EQUALS `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`
#ASSERT `ccc13 test the number of limbs` (`s 423.1(3) the punishments`) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `s 423.1(3) the class of the offence` EQUALS `an indictable offence`

§ `s 423.2 intimidation of health services`
#ASSERT `s 423.2(5) the person is a health professional` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 423.2(5) the person is a health professional` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- inputs of (1): conduct with the intent to provoke fear; the target; the health professional concerned (s 423.2(5))
#ASSERT `s 423.2(1) the conduct is the offence of intimidation of health services` TRUE `s 423.2(1) a person, in order to impede them from obtaining health services from a health professional` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 423.2(1) the conduct is the offence of intimidation of health services` TRUE `s 423.2(1) a health professional, in order to impede them in the performance of their duties` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 423.2(1) the conduct is the offence of intimidation of health services` TRUE `s 423.2(1) a person whose functions are to assist a health professional in the performance of the health professional’s duties, in order to impede that person in the performance of those functions` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 423.2(1) the conduct is the offence of intimidation of health services` TRUE `s 423.2(1) a health professional, in order to impede them in the performance of their duties` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE     -- not a health professional
#ASSERT `s 423.2(1) the conduct is the offence of intimidation of health services` TRUE `s 423.2(1) a target that is none of those` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 423.2(1) the conduct is the offence of intimidation of health services` FALSE `s 423.2(1) a health professional, in order to impede them in the performance of their duties` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 423.2(4) the person is saved from guilt of an offence under subsection (2)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 423.2(4) the person is saved from guilt of an offence under subsection (2)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 423.2(4) the person is saved from guilt of an offence under subsection (2)` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- inputs of (2): without lawful authority; intentionally obstructs or interferes; health professional (s 423.2(5)); the defence of (4)
#ASSERT `s 423.2(2) the conduct is the offence of obstructing access to health services` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 423.2(2) the conduct is the offence of obstructing access to health services` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE         -- the defence of (4)
#ASSERT `s 423.2(2) the conduct is the offence of obstructing access to health services` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 423.2(2) the conduct is the offence of obstructing access to health services` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE        -- not provided by a health professional
#ASSERT `s 423.2(2) the conduct is the offence of obstructing access to health services` FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 423.2(2) the conduct is the offence of obstructing access to health services` TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `ccc13 test the maximum imprisonment by indictment` (`s 423.2(3) the punishments` `ccc13 test p787`) EQUALS `imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`
#ASSERT `s 423.2(3) the class of the offence` EQUALS `ccc13 test the hybrid class`

§ `s 423.3 intimidation to impede access to a building used for religious worship, etc.`
`ccc13 test worship` MEANS `s 423.3(1) a building or structure, or part of a building or structure, that is primarily used for religious worship`
`ccc13 test the group's activities building` MEANS `s 423.3(1) a building or structure, or part of a building or structure, that is primarily used by an identifiable group for administrative, social, cultural or sports activities or events`
`ccc13 test the group's school` MEANS `s 423.3(1) a building or structure, or part of a building or structure, that is primarily used by an identifiable group as an educational institution, including a daycare centre`
`ccc13 test the group's seniors' residence` MEANS `s 423.3(1) a building or structure, or part of a building or structure, that is primarily used by an identifiable group as a residence for seniors`
-- inputs of (1): conduct with the intent to provoke fear in order to impede access to the place; the place; identifiable group (s 318(4))
#ASSERT `s 423.3(1) the conduct is the offence of intimidation to impede access to a building used for religious worship, etc.` TRUE `ccc13 test worship` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE         -- religious worship needs no identifiable group
#ASSERT `s 423.3(1) the conduct is the offence of intimidation to impede access to a building used for religious worship, etc.` TRUE `s 423.3(1) a cemetery` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 423.3(1) the conduct is the offence of intimidation to impede access to a building used for religious worship, etc.` TRUE `ccc13 test the group's activities building` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 423.3(1) the conduct is the offence of intimidation to impede access to a building used for religious worship, etc.` TRUE `ccc13 test the group's school` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 423.3(1) the conduct is the offence of intimidation to impede access to a building used for religious worship, etc.` TRUE `ccc13 test the group's seniors' residence` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 423.3(1) the conduct is the offence of intimidation to impede access to a building used for religious worship, etc.` TRUE `ccc13 test the group's school` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- not an identifiable group
#ASSERT `s 423.3(1) the conduct is the offence of intimidation to impede access to a building used for religious worship, etc.` TRUE `ccc13 test the group's school` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 423.3(1) the conduct is the offence of intimidation to impede access to a building used for religious worship, etc.` TRUE `s 423.3(1) a place that is none of those` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 423.3(1) the conduct is the offence of intimidation to impede access to a building used for religious worship, etc.` FALSE `ccc13 test worship` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 423.3(4) the person is saved from guilt of an offence under subsection (2)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 423.3(4) the person is saved from guilt of an offence under subsection (2)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- inputs of (2): without lawful authority; intentionally obstructs; the place is one of (1)(a) or a cemetery (s 423.3(1)); the exception of (4)
#ASSERT `s 423.3(2) the conduct is the offence of obstructing access to a building used for religious worship, etc.` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 423.3(2) the conduct is the offence of obstructing access to a building used for religious worship, etc.` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 423.3(2) the conduct is the offence of obstructing access to a building used for religious worship, etc.` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 423.3(2) the conduct is the offence of obstructing access to a building used for religious worship, etc.` FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `ccc13 test the maximum imprisonment by indictment` (`s 423.3(3) the punishments` `ccc13 test p787`) EQUALS `imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`
#ASSERT `s 423.3(3) the class of the offence` EQUALS `ccc13 test the hybrid class`

§ `s 424 and s 424.1 threats against internationally protected persons and United Nations personnel`
-- inputs of 424: threatens to commit the offence; the offence (by section number); the person threatened is an internationally protected person (s 2)
